    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16826" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ex-erro</span></b> , āre, v.
		n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to wander
				away</i> (post-Aug. and very rare). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dexterque exerrat Arion (equus),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 6, 444</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Anthol. Lat. 5, 172, 1</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">6, 17, 22</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to deviate</i>, <i>err</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">a via veritatis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cypr. Ep. 1, 12</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Sap. 12, 12</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mentibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 2
					Macc. 2, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
